    <methods>
      <methodStep>
        <description>
          <section>
            <title>Ethical Research Practices</title>
            <para>Drone pilots maintain an active Part 107 certification and followed all local airspace regulations. Work was conducted on land managed by either the Bureau of Land Management or Alaska Department of Natural Resources with the appropriate permitting and authorization. All equipment was removed from the field and efforts were made to limit the impacts of human travel across the tundra landscape. Work was not conducted over wildlife, human settlements, or people, except where affiliated with the flight team.</para>
          </section>
        </description>
      </methodStep>
      <methodStep>
        <description>
          <para>UAV flight(s) were conducted with a drone_v. gps_methrgb_meth ms_meth f_wx </para>
          <para>Contact uaf-iab-tfs-gis@alaska.edu for more information on methodology and data accuracy.</para>
		</description>
      </methodStep>
      <methodStep>
        <description>
          <para>Images were processed in Agisoft Metashape v2.2.1 or earlier using a standard photogrammetry workflow described in the Agisoft Metashape Users Manual (Agisoft LLC, 2022). The spatial resolution of the data products can be found in the Spatial Raster metadata below. Data products are in h_crs and NAVD88 Geoid12B (Alaska).</para>
        </description>
      </methodStep>
      <sampling>
